  "id": "Compound::DB00567 - Gene::213",
  "verbalization": "Cephalexin, a member of the cephalosporin class, is linked to Alb through a shared pathway involving cephalosporin antibiotics. The evidence suggests that Cephalexin, through its structural resemblance to Cefpiramide, ultimately binds to Cefotetan, which in turn interacts with Alb. This implies a potential mechanism where Cephalexin, via structural similarity, may influence the activity of Cefotetan, which then exerts a biological effect on Alb. The lowest common ancestors of these entities highlight a common pathway in the antibiotic class, reinforcing the idea of a functional relationship between Cephalexin and Alb through the cephalosporin family. The integration of these pathways suggests a possible role for Cephalexin in modulating the activity of Cefotetan, which may then affect Alb, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
